# KNCHA Backend

This is **Next.js 16** — read `node_modules/next/dist/docs/` before using APIs you are unsure about. See `AGENTS.md`.

## Repo purpose

Firebase-backed API + admin + mini `/play` client for football roster matching (F5/F7, Uruguay, 18+).

## Code standards

- **Minimize scope** — smallest correct diff; no unrelated refactors
- **Domain logic** in `src/lib/domain/*`, not only in route handlers
- **Validators** in `src/lib/validators/common.ts` (Zod)
- **Errors**: `ApiError` from `src/lib/errors.ts`; HTTP helpers in `src/lib/http.ts`
- **Types/constants** in `src/types/models.ts`
- **Language**: code/comments in English; user-facing strings may be Spanish

## Product rules (server-enforced)

+18 only; audience on events; invite=direct join; public=join request + poll; max 2 active events per organizer; poll closes 3h before start.

## Skills (read when relevant)

Project skills live in `.cursor/skills/`:

- `kncha-product` — business rules
- `kncha-api-endpoint` — new API routes
- `kncha-firebase` — Auth, Firestore, seeds
- `kncha-testing` — Vitest
- `kncha-git` — commits/PRs (no Cursor co-author)
- `kncha-ui-play-admin` — `/admin` and `/play` UI

## Keep skills in sync

After meaningful changes to product rules, API patterns, Firestore model, tests, or UI conventions, **check whether `.cursor/skills/` is outdated**. If it is, ask the user whether to update the relevant skill(s) in the same PR or a follow-up `chore(skills): ...` commit — do not update skills silently without asking.

## Git

Only commit when user asks. No `Co-authored-by: Cursor`. Use npm.
